  "id": "Compound::DB01224 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Quetiapine is implicated in the regulation of Cyp3a4 through a series of interconnected pathways involving agents that affect the nervous system. The evidence suggests that Quetiapine may influence Cyp3a4 via its interaction with other compounds that bind to this enzyme, such as Eszopiclone, Prochlorperazine, and Alfuzosin. These agents, all classified as organonitrogen heterocyclic compounds and agents affecting the nervous system, bind to Cyp3a4, potentially modulating its activity. The shared lowest common ancestors between Quetiapine and these agents—organonitrogen heterocyclic compounds and agents affecting the nervous system—suggest a broader functional relationship that may involve the enzyme's regulation in response to these compounds. The cumulative evidence points to a mechanism where Quetiapine indirectly influences Cyp3a4 through its interaction with these agents, which in turn bind to the enzyme, highlighting a potential role in the metabolic processing of these compounds.",
